-- title:
--   Coefficients of (f∣_kγ)(pτ) lie in ℚ(ζₚ)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$, let $k$ be an integer, and let $f$ be a modular form of weight $k$ for the subgroup $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$. Assume $f$ has integral $q$-expansion at $\infty$ in the sense that there is a power series $p_0$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose image under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{C}$ is the width-$1$ $q$-expansion of $f$. Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lie in $\Gamma_0(M)$ and satisfy $p \mid \gamma_{1,1}$, i.e. $p$ divides the lower right entry of $\gamma$. Consider the function on the upper half plane given by $\tau \mapsto (f \mid_k \gamma)(\mathrm{heckeDiagMatrix}(p) \cdot \tau)$, where $\mathrm{heckeDiagMatrix}(p)$ is the upper triangular matrix $\begin{pmatrix} p & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{pmatrix}$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ acting on $\tau$ by fractional linear transformation, so that the argument is $p\tau$. Then for every natural number $n$ the $n$-th coefficient of the width-$1$ $q$-expansion of this function lies in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{C}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by $\exp(2\pi i / p)$.
--
--   This is the rationality statement that the Atkin–Lehner operator at $p$ on forms of level $Mp$, $p \nmid M$, is defined over the cyclotomic field $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ when coefficients are taken with respect to the $q$-expansion at the cusp $\infty$. It is used in the construction of the degeneracy/Atkin–Lehner correspondences between the curves $X_1(Mp)$ and $X_0(M)$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.exists_sum_smul_eq_smul_atkinLehnerSlash_gamma1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_sum_smul_eq_smul_atkinLehnerSlash_gamma1_mul) and [`ModularCurve.exists_sum_smul_eq_smul_atkinLehnerSlash_x1x0_gamma0`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_sum_smul_eq_smul_atkinLehnerSlash_x1x0_gamma0).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_qExpansion_coeff_atkinLehnerSlash_mem_adjoin_exp_gamma1_mul.lean

import Mathlib
